<p>The State Department and a U.S. official confirmed Tuesday that Julie Davis, the acting U.S. ambassador and chargé d’affaires in Kyiv, will leave Kyiv in June 2026 and retire from the State Department. Accounts differ over why she is leaving: Financial Times reporting pointed to differences with President Trump’s Ukraine policy, while the State Department rejected that explanation. The announcement came as U.S.-brokered talks on a ceasefire and an end to Russia’s invasion of Ukraine remained stalled.</p><img src='https://kagiproxy.com/img/ottxRoVc7No0_JlU8bGIqlGPzK7kELc1Fnnq3k0xdon_HpMoCxHod_1blwJRFmrRhUopX9uvRD1XSxsfB7jiRX2wMMdo7R2qnVoJmK6d4k-XnFxAOjaj-3Bu9BHSi6eCColTPOjwmIU6b7fGM8x9NfCRTDAGpyUak-BWPVPAYyo0uUHUpM9xKyZAnDOZvbn8UjQ-pPJ7aVyCSnSwoI-5isGDUjPFh9WQtkdTwF5MChQDzxQ91w_1qyC2fzfG4vb5DLbC2yCRy1zgZU1xpA' alt='Julie Davis, acting U.S. ambassador to Ukraine, attends a session of the Ukrainian parliament in Kyiv in May 2025.' /><br /><h3>Highlights:</h3><ul><li>Davis is leaving after less than a year leading the U.S. mission in Kyiv.</li><li>Reports cited Russian preparations for a summer offensive in discussing the potential consequences of a leadership gap at the U.S. Embassy.</li><li>As chargé d’affaires, Davis was the acting head of the U.S. mission rather than a Senate-confirmed ambassador.</li></ul><blockquote>Ambassador Davis has been a steadfast proponent of the Trump administration’s efforts to bring about a durable peace between Russia and Ukraine - Tommy Pigott</blockquote><h3>Perspectives:</h3><ul><li>State Department: Pigott said claims that Davis was leaving over disagreements with Trump were inaccurate and said she supported the administration’s Russia-Ukraine peace effort. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639234-us-envoy-ukraine-resigns/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Financial Times sources: People familiar with the matter said Davis’ frustration centered on what they described as reduced U.S. backing for Kyiv. (<a href='https://www.ft.com/content/33d5d8d4-a7db-4647-9751-c21de8ebecb8'>Financial Times</a>)</li><li>Bridget Brink: Davis’ predecessor wrote after resigning that U.S. policy had pressured Ukraine, which she called the victim, rather than Russia, which she called the aggressor. (<a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639234-us-envoy-ukraine-resigns/'>RT</a>)</li><li>Volodymyr Zelenskyy: Zelenskyy told Reuters in March that the Trump administration tied security guarantees for Ukraine to a peace treaty under which Ukraine would cede the Donbas to Russia, an arrangement he opposed. (<a href='https://444.hu/2026/04/29/inkabb-nyugdijba-vonul-a-legmagasabb-rangu-amerikai-diplomata-kijevben-annyira-elege-van-trumpbol'>444.hu</a>)</li></ul><h3>Sources:</h3><ul><li><a href='https://www.scmp.com/news/world/russia-central-asia/article/3351766/trumps-ukraine-envoy-stepping-down-amid-stalled-peace-talks-russia'>Trump’s Ukraine envoy stepping down amid stalled peace talks with Russia</a> - scmp.com</li><li><a href='https://www.straitstimes.com/world/united-states/us-ambassador-to-ukraine-to-step-down-amid-stalled-talks-to-end-ukraine-war'>US ambassador to Ukraine to step down amid stalled talks to end Ukraine war</a> - straitstimes.com</li><li><a href='https://www.rt.com/news/639234-us-envoy-ukraine-resigns/'>US envoy to Ukraine to resign over disagreements with Trump – FT</a> - rt.com</li><li><a href='https://www.theglobeandmail.com/world/article-us-ambassador-ukraine-kyiv-russia-trump/'>U.S. ambassador to Ukraine steps down due to frustration with Trump, reports say</a> - theglobeandmail.com</li><li><a href='https://www.ft.com/content/33d5d8d4-a7db-4647-9751-c21de8ebecb8'>US ambassador to Ukraine to leave over differences with Trump</a> - ft.com</li><li><a href='https://english.nv.ua/nation/u-s-charge-d-affaires-in-ukraine-to-leave-post-50603899.html'>U.S. chargé d’affaires to leave post over disagreements with Trump — FT</a> - nv.ua</li><li><a href='https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/apr/29/us-ambassador-ukraine-trump-st